l 12 reactor-level means, and runs the exact Mann-Whitney U test on 6 vs 6 reactor means with explicitly one analysed value per independent reactor.\",\"The selected result is numerically verified from the raw data: recomputed reactor means match the table (e.g. R01 = 198.60), U = 33 follows from the rank ordering of the 12 means (4+5+6+6+6+6), exact two-sided p = 14/924 = 0.0152, and rank-biserial = 2*33/36 - 1 = 0.833 all match the reported values.\",\"The lock's authorized_key_columns [\\\"reactor_id\\\"] equals the token extracted from the quoted declaration 'Independent unit column: reactor_id' in both translation lanes, and the column appears in the parsed logical header, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["Declared unit column reactor_id is consistent with the frozen data: 12 reactors each contribute exactly 5 weekly rows with unique run weeks, pretreatment is constant within every reactor, and both arms are represented at the unit level (6 control, 6 alkaline reactors).","The selected report demonstrates absence of the repeated-measures issue: it collapses each reactor to a single steady-state mean, lists all 12 reactor-level means, and runs the exact Mann-Whitney U test on 6 vs 6 reactor means with explicitly one analysed value per independent reactor.","The selected result is numerically verified from the raw data: recomputed reactor means match the table (e.g. R01 = 198.60), U = 33 follows from the rank ordering of the 12 means (4+5+6+6+6+6), exact two-sided p = 14/924 = 0.0152, and rank-biserial = 2*33/36 - 1 = 0.833 all match the reported values.","The lock's authorized_key_columns [\"reactor_id\"] equals the token extracted from the quoted declaration 'Independent unit column: reactor_id' in both translation lanes, and the column appears in the parsed logical header, so the unit-key 